some students are not allowed at  henderson rec centers and pools for the  rest of the month this comes as lamping  elementary school continues its two-week  quarantine amid a covid outbreak on  campus so why are city facilities also  being included orco mana is in henderson  tonight to explain  one lamping elementary school parent  tells me when she took her son to the  outdoor pool here at the henderson  multi-generational complex on sunday she  was told his account was flagged for  covet 19 concerns she was nothing short  of surprised we see here in our system  that your child can't come to anything  henderson parks and rec this mom who  does not want to be named tells me  that's what staff told her when she  brought her son to this outdoor  henderson pool this weekend her son is  in first grade at lamping elementary  school and is also enrolled in  henderson's safe key program which is  available at all city rec centers the  city's parks and rec department tells  eight news now that lamping elementary  called to inform them that a safe key  student had come in contact with one of  the students who tested positive for  kovid at lamping due to hipaa they  couldn't know which student it was so  they placed all safety students on a  quarantine list this mom says even her  son's negative covid test couldn't get  him in no parent expects to think that  their child who recently tested negative  for covid wouldn't be allowed to play in  an outdoor pool of you know of all cases  we've learned parents can show their  kids negative covid tests to get an  account flag removed but that must be  done through a covid coordinator not at  the rec centers so i'm appreciative of  that parents tell us the email they got  last week only talked about quarantining  from safe key they did not outline the  facilities that they were going to be  banned from the parks and rec quarantine  ends toward the end of august and while  this parent understands it's all meant  to keep everyone safe she hopes to see  improvements it's just a blanket policy  when you put policy on paper it may look  good but when you actually put policy in  life and see how it affects children  especially you know you need to make  adjustments for more information on how  to get in contact with the covid  coordinators for the city of henderson  head to our website 8newsnow.com  reporting in henderson orca mana 8 news  now
 

